## Results — Proof of Connectivity

### ✅ Both VPN Tunnels UP on AWS Console
```
Tunnel 1: 3.211.251.140 → UP ✅
Tunnel 2: 3.230.7.122   → UP ✅
```

### ✅ VTI Interface Active on StrongSwan
```bash
ip addr show vti1
# vti1@NONE: <POINTOPOINT,NOARP,UP,LOWER_UP>
# link/ipip 192.168.1.148 peer 3.211.251.140
```

### ✅ Route Through Tunnel
```bash
ip route show | grep vti1
# 10.0.0.0/16 dev vti1 scope link
```

### ✅ Ping: On-Prem Private → AWS Private
```bash
# From 192.168.2.149:
ping 10.0.1.207 -c 5
# 64 bytes from 10.0.1.207: icmp_seq=1 ttl=124 time=2.22ms
# 64 bytes from 10.0.1.207: icmp_seq=2 ttl=124 time=2.28ms
# 64 bytes from 10.0.1.207: icmp_seq=3 ttl=124 time=2.08ms
# 64 bytes from 10.0.1.207: icmp_seq=4 ttl=124 time=2.42ms
# 64 bytes from 10.0.1.207: icmp_seq=5 ttl=124 time=2.15ms
# 0% packet loss ✅
```

### ✅ Ping: AWS Private → On-Prem Private
```bash
# From 10.0.1.207:
ping 192.168.2.149 -c 5
# 64 bytes from 192.168.2.149 ✅
# 0% packet loss ✅
```

